PRINCIPLES AND OBJECTIVES
Article 2
The Principles of Implementation of Protection for Victims of Gender-Based Violence and Children are: non-discrimination;
best interests of victims;
justice and gender equality;
victim protection;
survival and development of children;
respect for the views of children;
transparency;
integration;
empowerment; and confidentiality of victims.

Article 15
Return Services as referred to in Article 9 letter f include: return of victims of gender-based violence and child victims;
return of victims of the criminal act of trafficking in persons.
Social Reintegration Services as referred to in Article 9 letter f include: reintegration with the family;
reintegration with a substitute family;
reintegration with the community environment; and educational reintegration.

Article 16
Coordination and cooperation as referred to in Article 9 letter g includes: conducting coordination and cooperation in handling cases of violence with UPPTK;
conducting coordination and cooperation with integrated service centers between regencies/cities; and conducting coordination and cooperation with institutions providing services for victims of gender-based violence and children.
